Track 1: "Does the Foghorn Bleed?"
- Story & Context: Devika dragged her rusted teardrop sitar past the salt-crusted parapet of Spire 9 just as black floodwater began churning through the 79th-floor service grates. As the city squall sirens shorted out in the storm, Jax cracked an iron rebar against an empty freon cylinder, venting a sour cloud of coolant into a shivering crowd of three hundred drowned-dock refugees. When police patrol skiffs turned sweeping searchlights toward the rooftop, the band didn't run; they slammed into an overdriven 432Hz modal drone so physically massive that the harbor patrol mistook the acoustic blast for an industrial hull fracture, while Devika screamed through a megaphone, "Drink the brine before it drinks your lungs."
