Track 2: The Ballast Sweats Copper
- Story & Context: Crouched in the leaking utility crawlspace beneath the heli-deck, bassist Sorab spliced frayed copper sitar wire directly into an exposed bilge-pump solenoid while untreated trench-rot throbbed in his boots with every cold slap of seafoam. He remembered trading his younger sister’s dry-dock grain allotment to buy three surplus vacuum tubes from an offshore smuggler whose pilot-cabin stank of clove cigarettes and stale diesel. The guilt hummed inside the track’s crawling, three-chord sludge, shaking crusted salt flakes from the speaker mesh until Sorab dropped his head against the hot amplifier casing and wept into the mic, "I traded your bread for copper thunder."
