Track 3: Pani-Ghar Shoal-Run
- Story & Context: By sunrise, Spire 9 had become an acoustic beacon, its drowned concrete elevator core vibrating with sympathetic sitar overtones long after the Coast Guard’s grappling hooks had severed the rooftop generator lines. Deep-water salvage divers navigating the sunken avenues still tune their helmet radios to the resonant frequency of the flooded tower, swearing that the salt-water masonry absorbed the final chord of that solstice morning and never stopped humming it back to the seabed. A stubborn legend took root across the barge-city slums that the band never evacuated the building, leaving only Jax’s cracked crash cymbal wedged into a drainage pipe that still shudders in the tide, "No dry ground left to bury our screams."
